    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50108" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερόσῡλ-ος</span></b> , ὁ,
		(proparox.) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>temple-robber</i>,
			or generally, <i>sacrilegious person</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				30.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				344b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				560
			</span></i>, etc.: fem., ib.<i><span class="en">
				504
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερόσυλε γραῦ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				524
			</span></i>: neut. as Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. θηρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pk.</u>
					176
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>got by sacrilege</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παροψίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eub.
					7.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
